Installing Potato Make
======================

Requirements
------------

  - GNU Guile 3.0 or 2.2, with its development files
    (the package is called guile-3.0-dev on Debian and Ubuntu,
    and guile30-devel on Fedora)
  - make

and, only when building from a Git checkout rather than from a
release tarball,

  - Autoconf, Automake, and pkg-config
  - Texinfo

Building
--------

From a Git checkout, first generate the configure script:

    autoreconf -vif

Then, the usual commands apply:

    ./configure
    make
    make check
    make install

The Scheme modules are installed in

    PREFIX/share/guile/site/GUILE_VERSION/potato

and the compiled modules in

    PREFIX/lib/guile/GUILE_VERSION/site-ccache/potato

where PREFIX is /usr/local unless you pass --prefix to configure.
Guile only searches the directories beneath its own prefix.  If Guile
is installed in /usr, either configure with

    ./configure --prefix=/usr

or add the two directories above to the GUILE_LOAD_PATH and
GUILE_LOAD_COMPILED_PATH environment variables.

Pass --disable-guild to configure to install the modules without
byte-compiling them.

Using Potato Make without installing it
---------------------------------------

After running make, the pre-inst-env script runs a command with the
uninstalled modules on Guile's load path:

    ./pre-inst-env guile -s examples/hello.scm

Documentation
-------------

The manual is installed in Info format.  To build it in HTML format,
run

    make html

which creates doc/potato-make.html/index.html.
